},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The chunks, each up to a few kilobytes of elements, are the vertices of an AVL tree in flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrays, in sequence order, and each vertex records how many elements its subtree holds, so an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"offset is found from the root in O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") (Boehm, Atkinson and Plass, “Ropes: an Alternative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to Strings”, 1995). Each chunk is its own copy-on-write buffer: a copy of a rope shares every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chunk with the original until one of them edits it, and appending one rope to another shares"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the appended rope’s chunks."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var text = Rope(\"Hello, world!\")","text.insert(contentsOf: \"brave new \", at: 7)","String(text)                       \/\/ \"Hello, brave new world!\"","text.removeSubrange(5 ..< 16)","String(text)                       \/\/ \"Hello world!\"","text[6]                            \/\/ \"w\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Indices are offsets from the start, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< count"},{"type":"text","text":". Reading an element costs O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(1) amortized over a pass through the rope."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Ropes/documentation/Ropes/Rope/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations":{"title":"CustomStringConvertible Impl